  "notes": "{親|した}しい is an i-adjective meaning \"close\" or \"intimate\" in relationships.\n\nFORMS:\n- Negative: {親|した}しくない\n- Adverb: {親|した}しく\n- Noun form: {親|した}しさ (closeness)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {親|した}しい{友人|ゆうじん}: close friend\n- {親|した}しい{仲|なか}: intimate relationship\n- {親|した}しい{間柄|あいだがら}: close relationship\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {親|した}しむ (verb): to become familiar with, to enjoy\n- {親|した}しみ (noun): familiarity, friendliness\n- {親|した}しみやすい: approachable, friendly\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\n{親|した}しい describes emotional closeness between people. For physical proximity, use {近|ちか}い instead.",
